{"caption":"A right hand pinches a Staples CD-RW disc by its rim above a dark wooden tabletop, holding the label side toward the camera while a green Staples jewel case rests in the lower-left corner. The viewpoint and background stay fixed as the disc undergoes small, slow tilts, keeping the STAPLES CD-RW text legible while a rainbow sheen drifts across the white label surface.

The hand then tilts the disc more strongly toward the light, so the printed label washes into a bright overexposed glare and the circular outline visibly foreshortens into an ellipse. The disc passes briefly and motion-blurred nearly edge-on before continuing its slow rotation onward. Its reflective data side then fills the view, showing dark mirror-like surfaces crossed by strong, bright spectral rainbow diffraction bands.

Throughout the flip, the thumb remains at the lower right and fingers at the top. The lower-left jewel case and wood-grain background do not shift, showing the change comes from disc tilt rather than camera motion.","length_note":""}
